            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="BRO08" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>George</forename>
                        <surname>Brodie</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1786">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1867"/>
                    <occupation>Historian</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin distinguishes a few entries in fair number to 'Brodie', which we
                            have mostly attributed to Eilliam Bird Brodie the Salisbury bookseller
                            and MP, to 'G. Brodie.' This looks likely to be George Brodie the
                            historian of the History of the British Empire from Accession of Charles
                            I to Restoration' - a topic close to Godwin's interests in the
                            Commonwealth, and he can be seen reading the book in 1822 and (we
                            judge), then writing to G. Brodie (in 1822 and 1823) who was based in
                            Scotland (for at least some time - he moved to London at some point only
                            after his marriage in 1823), to relay his views. </p><p>There is a
                            brither, Alexander Brodie (1785-1858), who wrote a history of the Roman
                            Republic, but we think was not resident in England.</p>
                    </note>
